    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2UaawFPJPpc6GEfudChCEah)_\n\nEmacs 31.1 marks `when-let` and `if-let` obsolete. This renames all 34 uses in `libraries/modules/` and the matching code in `docs/tangles/` (the canonical `.org` files) to `when-let*` / `if-let*`, plus the one prose mention in `sp-graphs.org`. There were no `and-let` uses.\n\nEvery site already used the double-parenthesis binding list `((VAR EXPR))`, which the starred macros accept unchanged, so no binding lists needed rewrapping. The only change per site is the added `*`. `.el` and `.org` were edited identically, so the tangled output stays in sync. `libraries/themes/` and `cloned/` were not touched (they had no uses). `CHANGELOG.org` has a line under \"Startup, load order and configuration hygiene\".\n\n**Checked:** grep finds no remaining `when-let`, `if-let` or `and-let` without a star under `libraries/` and `docs/`; the diff is 68 lines changed with an identical number added and removed, and only the `*` differs, so bracket balance is unchanged. **Not run:** no Emacs in this environment, so nothing was byte-compiled or loaded.\n\n---\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01BVEYEfHZ2wHtBvcihjsSPx)_",
